# Semi-Automated Sales Pipeline

## Purpose
Increase the volume of outreach while tracking lead behavior across email campaigns.

The goal was to combine automation with manual control, allowing the sales team to handle edge cases and personalize outreach when needed.

---

## Business Problem
We lacked a clear structure for tracking leads across the sales process:

- No clear overview of which leads had already been contacted  
- Difficult to track where each lead was in the pipeline  
- Manual process for identifying “warm leads”  
- Risk of missing follow-ups and potential deals  

---

## Solution
Built a semi-automated pipeline connecting campaign data with a structured sales workflow.

---

## Tools & Systems
- CRM / Outreach: Lemlist  
- Data layer: Google Sheets  
- Sales pipeline: Trello  
- Automation: Google Apps Script (API integrations & scheduled jobs)  

---

## Simplified Flow
Lead → Campaign → Engagement Tracking → Lead Scoring → Sales Board → Follow-up  

---

## Automation & Data Processing
- Campaign and lead data fetched via API  
- Data processed and stored in Google Sheets  
- Leads evaluated based on engagement behavior  
- Trello cards created/updated automatically for warm leads  
- Sync runs every hour (Mon–Fri, 08:00–19:00)  

---

## Lead Scoring Logic
A lead is considered “warm” if:

- ≥ 3 email opens  
- OR ≥ 1 click  
- OR ≥ 1 reply  

---

## Key Data Points
- Name  
- Campaign activity (opens, clicks, replies)  
- Trello card URL  

---

